.TH DANBY-CROSSINFECTION 1
.SH NAME
danby-crossinfection \- infection transmitted within and between two species
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B danby/crossinfection
.SH MODEL
The force of infection on species A is beta IA+k IB; that on species B is
beta IB+k IA.  Each force transfers its susceptible compartment to infectious,
and infectious members recover at species-specific rates.  Recovered members
leave the four displayed active compartments.
.SH DISPLAY
Four histories distinguish the susceptible and infectious populations of both
species.  Cross contact can synchronize otherwise different outbreaks.
.SH CONTROLS
Drag any compartment bar.  Tracks set within-species contact, cross-species
contact, and both recovery rates.  Space pauses, period steps, r resets, and
q exits.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/danby/plugin/crossinfection.b
.br
.B /appl/danby/crossinfection.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR populationmodel (2),
.IR danby-malaria (1)
